  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: D</p>\n<p>A: Incorrect. This is far below the equilibrium temperature obtained from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\\sigma T^4=(1-\\alpha)S\"></span>.</p>\n<p>B: Incorrect. This is far below the equilibrium temperature obtained from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\\sigma T^4=(1-\\alpha)S\"></span>.</p>\n<p>C: Incorrect. This is far below the equilibrium temperature obtained from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\\sigma T^4=(1-\\alpha)S\"></span>.</p>\n<p>D: Correct. Absorbed flux: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{abs}}=(1-\\alpha)S=0.80\\times1500=1200\\ \\mathrm{W\\,m^{-2}}\"></span>. Equate to emitted flux: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{\\text{emit}}=\\varepsilon\\sigma T^4=0.6(5.67\\times10^{-8})T^4\"></span>. So <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T^4=\\dfrac{1200}{0.6\\times5.67\\times10^{-8}}\\approx3.53\\times10^{10}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\\approx(3.53\\times10^{10})^{1/4}\\approx4.33\\times10^2\\ \\mathrm{K}\"></span>.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A planet receives solar radiation at a rate of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1500\\ \\mathrm{W\\,m^{-2}}\"></span> and has an albedo of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.20\"></span>. If the emissivity of the surface is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.6\"></span>, what is the approximate equilibrium temperature of the planet?</p>\n<p>(<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sigma = 5.67 \\times 10^{-8}\\ \\mathrm{W\\,m^{-2}\\,K^{-4}}\"></span>)</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"240\\ \\mathrm{K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"263\\ \\mathrm{K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"278\\ \\mathrm{K}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"433\\ \\mathrm{K}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
